  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently focused on defining the project scope, specifically for \"Sistem Informasi Akademik (SIAKAD) V1 \342\200\223 Madrasah Inovatif (MI Miftahul Khoir 1 Karangrejo)\". Right now, my thinking is centered on it being a Single Page Application (SPA). I\'ve started outlining the essential roles: Admin and Guru.\n\n\n**Refining the Integration Strategy**\n\nI\'m rethinking the architecture. Originally, I envisioned a backend-less SPA leveraging local storage and simulated Google Sheets/Apps Script interactions for the \"Sistem Informasi Akademik\". However, the guidelines conflict with this approach. Now, I must integrate real functionality. This makes me consider how to connect to real services and handle user data within the constraints of the project. I need to focus on genuine integrations and address preview limitations in the documentation. The project is still an SPA.\n\n\n**Considering Dual Modes**\n\nI\'ve hit on a really great idea for the Google ecosystem integration. My plan now is to create a dual-mode system. There will be a fully functional, out-of-the-box application that leverages local storage and realistic, pre-populated data. Alongside this, I\'ll provide an interactive panel for Admin/Guru. This panel will display the Apps Script code, provide setup instructions for connecting to real Google Sheets, and allow users to input their Apps Script Web App URL for live data integration! It\'s both robust and flexible.\n\n\n**Implementing Web App Integration**\n\nNow, I\'m thinking about the direct integration with Google Apps Script Web Apps. If the user provides their Web App URL, I\'ll allow the application to make `fetch` calls, reading and writing Google Sheet data. I\'ll provide the complete Apps Script code for them to copy and paste. I\'m focusing on aligning perfectly with the goal of \"Build real integrations\" and \"Guide configuration\". The preview limits are also being addressed. Let\'s start with the skills and technologies required for this project! I will have to start by reviewing the skills.\n\n\n**Analyzing Skill Set Requirements**\n\nI\'ve just finished a skill check and the `gemini-api` is not explicitly requested. My current thinking aligns directly with the user\'s SIAKAD V1 requirements (attendance, journals, reports, printing) and I\'m planning to keep the approach simple. I reviewed the available skills, eliminating those irrelevant to this SPA project, and focusing on the core integration needs.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
