  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Development Script**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the development script, specifically examining how the application is being launched. The script `\"dev\": \"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\"` clearly indicates a Client-Side SPA using Vite, running on port 3000 and accessible via all host interfaces. This suggests a specific runtime environment handling the SPA automatically.\n\n\n**Refining the Application Concept**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve confirmed this is a client-side only React app. Excellent! I\'m now fully immersed in envisioning the application\'s aesthetic. I\'m leaning towards a modern Islamic design with a green/mint primary palette, accented by soft dark slate or elegant warm cream, suitable for the target Madrasah. The goal is a professional, clean visual experience, consistent with the school\'s identity. I\'m also planning to utilize Tailwind CSS and `motion` for polished animations.\n\n\n**Defining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now determining the visual components, and I\'ve locked down the color palette! For the primary design, I plan to use Tailwind classes like `emerald-600`, `emerald-700`, and `emerald-50`, then `teal-900`. I\'m also thinking of golden-bronze accents like `amber-500` or `yellow-500` to portray excellence. I\'m focusing on clean layouts, beautiful typography with \'Inter\' body font and \'Outfit\', a classy modern geometric font, for the headers.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Planning Authentication and RBAC**\n\nI\'m deep in thought on authentication and RBAC now. I\'m designing three core roles: Admin, Teacher, and Student. Admins get full dashboard access, attendance rekap data, log reviews, and synchronization panels. Teachers get attendance verification, daily journal features, and reports, with attendance editing capabilities. Students get read-only access to their attendance records, stats, card scanner logs, and alerts. I\'ll provide standard accounts to click and test the different role permissions.\n\n\n**Designing User Roles and Flows**\n\nI\'m now implementing the authentication flow and considering user personas. I\'ll include several user accounts with roles: Guru (teacher), Admin, and Murid (student) for testing. I\'m focusing on a highly responsive login page with role switcher buttons for quick testing. I\'m also preparing a mock dataset for Kelas 5A students to simulate the attendance verification module. The teacher will be able to mark attendance with different statuses (Hadir, Izin, Sakit, Alpa) displayed with different colors, showing instant attendance metrics.\n\n\n**Implementing the Journal Feature**\n\nI\'m now implementing the daily journal feature for teachers. I will store the journal data using the following fields: date (prefilled with today\'s date), class (e.g., 5A), subject (e.g., Fiqih), material taught (text input), and special notes (text area). I\'m also including a \"Save Journal & Attendance Snapshot\" button that saves the journal entry and appends the daily attendance metrics. I\'ll provide full edit and delete capabilities, with the embedded attendance snapshot always preserved, for review.\n\n\n**Generating the Report View**\n\nI\'m now integrating date filters for attendance and journal data. I will be incorporating \"Tanggal Mulai\" and \"Tanggal Selesai\" input fields, and a class filter. I plan to present a comprehensive table showing attendance percentages and counts (presence, sick, excuse, alpa) per student. A second table will display the submitted journal entries. I\'ve built in a \"Cetak Laporan / Print\" button to trigger the browser\'s print function, and I\'m currently focused on critical CSS print styling.\n\n\n**Integrating the Data Source**\n\nI\'m now integrating Google Apps Script as the backend. I will add a URL input field, a \"Check Connection\" button, and detailed setup instructions for the Google Sheet. I\'ll also provide the complete Apps Script code for handling data fetching and saving, making live API requests to synchronize the data with the React app. I plan to organize the project into directories like `/src/types.ts`, `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`, `/src/components/Login.tsx`, and `/src/components/VerifikasiAbsensi.tsx`.\n\n\n**Structuring the Project Files**\n\nI\'m now establishing the file structure. I\'m focusing on modularity, and I\'ve started populating `/metadata.json` with the application name, \"SIAKAD MI Miftahul Khoir 1,\" and a description: \"Sistem Informasi Akademik Madrasah Inovatif Miftahul Khoir 1 Karangrejo - Verifikasi Presensi, Jurnal Guru, & Cetak Rekapitulasi.\" My next step is organizing the core components in `/src/components`. I\'ll make the following: `JurnalHarian.tsx`, `CetakLaporan.tsx`, `IntegrationPanel.tsx`, `DashboardMurid.tsx`, `DashboardAdmin.tsx`, and `App.tsx` files. I\'m aiming for clean imports and export statements!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 497000033
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
