  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Completion**\n\nI\'m pleased to report a successful build! Now, I\'m meticulously cross-referencing the project requirements to ensure complete implementation. I\'m focusing on the single-page application aspects, specifically its cross-role functionality (Admin, Teacher, Student) and its lightweight, nested structure. I\'m double-checking for any overlooked files or unaddressed features.\n\n\n**Completed Key Integrations**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated LocalStorage and Google Sheets/Apps Script for dual support. Furthermore, I\'ve fully populated student states with NFC data and created an interactive \"NFC Tap Simulation\". Now, I\'ve digitized the daily teacher journal process, automatically embedding attendance stats, with full history, edit/delete capabilities! Finally, the printing/reporting feature based on a specific time range is working, and the data is filterable.\n\n\n**Finalizing Print Functionality**\n\nI\'ve finalized print-ready tables using `tsx`, complete with date and class filters, enabling output of student attendance and lesson journals. I\'ve also implemented a \"Cetak Laporan / Print\" button. I\'m especially proud of the \"VerifikasiAbsensi.tsx\" implementation, allowing teachers to see today\'s NFC attendance at a glance. They can also override NFC data, flagging anomalies like \"titip absen\" with a clear red notice for absolute data integrity. Finally, time-range based reports can be generated.\n\n\n**Refining Output & Access**\n\nI\'ve added custom print-CSS in `src/index.css` for professional letterhead formatting and official sign-off lines, creating polished print results. A pupil\'s read-only attendance history is now accessible within `DashboardMurid.tsx`, helping them monitor their own discipline. I\'ve also implemented easy credential entry, with an interactive Quick-Login Panel for seamless role switching during testing.\n\n\n"
